## roar (provenance tracker)

This project uses [roar](https://github.com/treqs/roar) to capture lineage for ML/data pipeline runs.

- **Run scripts with provenance:** prefer `roar run <cmd>` over bare `<cmd>` (e.g. `roar run python train.py`).
- **Don't modify code to use roar.** Capture is transparent. The exception: `from roar import require` at the top of a script aborts if it isn't being run under `roar run`.
- **Clean git state is required.** `roar run` refuses to execute with uncommitted changes (including untracked files). No `--dirty` bypass. Make sure `.roar/` is in `.gitignore`.
- **One commit for the whole pipeline.** Don't commit between steps: `roar reproduce` checks out the last commit, so a session spanning several replays earlier steps against code they never ran with. Iterate freely, then commit once and run the publishable pipeline end-to-end without touching a tracked file.
- **Publishing is separate from capture.** `roar scope use <org>/<project>` sets the destination; `roar register --dry-run` previews the reproducibility checklist and secret scan without publishing; `roar register` publishes. `--anonymous` discards attribution irreversibly — don't use it unless anonymity is the goal.
- **Name what you publish.** `roar run -n "train model"` names a step; `roar label set artifact <path> name=... description=... license.id=...` names a model and fills its AI-BOM fields. Unnamed lineage reads publicly as `python3 train.py` producing `model.pkl`.
- **Avoid `/tmp` for workdirs.** Default config has `ignore_tmp_files = true`, which drops intermediates written under `/tmp`; a `/tmp` file the run only reads is kept but flagged unsourced (see below).
- **Mind unsourced inputs.** An input with no tracked producer that isn't committed to git — a manual download, a `/tmp` file, an uncommitted script — won't exist when the run is reproduced elsewhere, and is the most common reason a lineage doesn't reproduce. List them with `roar inputs --unsourced <ref>`; fix by committing code or ingesting data with `roar get <url>` (or `roar run wget <url>`).
- **Inspect lineage:** `roar show <ref>`, `roar log`, `roar dag`. Add `--all` to `roar show` to disable truncation.
- **Don't commit `.roar/`** — it's local lineage state.
- **`roar --help` is the source of truth** for current command behavior.
